 P(y=c\mid x)=\text{softmax}(z)_c=\frac{e^{z_c}}{\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{C}e^{z_k}}
 }

blocks.cap:
Softmax on three sets of scores. Close scores give a flat distribution;
 a clear winner gives a peaked one; equal scores give exactly $1/3$ each. The
 probabilities always sum to 1.

blocks.t:
\text{softmax}(z+a\mathbf{1})_c
 =\frac{e^{z_c+a}}{\sum_k e^{z_k+a}}
 =\frac{e^{a}e^{z_c}}{e^{a}\sum_k e^{z_k}}
 =\text{softmax}(z)_c .

\boxed{ 
 L=-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{c=1}^{C} y_{ic}\log \left(p_{ic}\right)
 }

\frac{\partial L}{\partial z_c}=p_c-y_c
 \qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad
 \boxed{ \nabla_{W}L=\frac{1}{n}\left(P-Y\right)^{ \top}X }
